<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_Margin @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_Margin @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</h1>


<p>
    Everything you need to work with the <span class="br-code-span">br-margin-*</span> CSS classes: the utility classes provided, the strongly-typed <span class="br-code-span">Margin</span> C# object
    used to apply them, and the supporting enum used to select a spacing value.
</p>

<h2 class="page-heading">Overview</h2>

<p>
    <span class="br-code-span">Margin</span> is a <b>utility class</b>, not a BEM component class like <span class="br-code-span">Section</span> or <span class="br-code-span">Button</span>.
    Rather than describing a block, element, or its variants, each class here sets a single CSS property to a fixed value from the shared <span class="br-code-span">--br-unit-space-*</span>
    spacing scale, plus a small set of fixed <span class="br-code-span">auto</span> margin classes. Utility classes are flat and single-purpose by design, so they can be freely combined
    with each other and with any other class - including component classes - on the same element.
</p>
<p>
    Because they read directly from the <span class="br-code-span">--br-unit-space-*</span> primitives - values that rarely change once a theme is set - these classes are not
    part of the <span class="br-code-span">--br-cls-*</span> theme-reactive colour layer described on other pages.
</p>
<p>
    Unlike <span class="br-code-span">Padding</span>, <span class="br-code-span">Margin</span> also provides fixed <span class="br-code-span">auto</span> classes.
    <span class="br-code-span">padding: auto</span> is not valid CSS, so no equivalent exists on the <span class="br-code-span">Padding</span> class.
</p>

<section>
    <h2 id="c#-classes" class="page-heading">C# API</h2>
    <p>
        <span class="br-code-span">Margin</span> provides utility classes that set margin from the <span class="br-code-span">--br-unit-space-*</span> primitive scale, plus fixed
        <span class="br-code-span">auto</span> margin classes.
    </p>
    <section class="code-table">
        <h3 id="margin-class" class="code-table__heading">Margin class</h3>
        <table aria-labelledby="margin-class">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Return</th>
                    <th scope="col">Const/Static Method</th>
                    <th scope="col">Description</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Margin.AutoInline</td>
                    <td>Centres the element horizontally by setting inline-direction margin to <span class="br-code-span">auto</span>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Margin.AutoBlock</td>
                    <td>Sets block-direction margin to <span class="br-code-span">auto</span>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Margin.Auto</td>
                    <td>Sets margin to <span class="br-code-span">auto</span> on all sides.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Margin.All(UnitSpace unitSpace)</td>
                    <td>Gets the class that sets margin on all sides.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Margin.Inline(UnitSpace unitSpace)</td>
                    <td>Gets the class that sets inline-direction (left/right in LTR) margin.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Margin.InlineStart(UnitSpace unitSpace)</td>
                    <td>Gets the class that sets inline-start (left in LTR) margin.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Margin.InlineEnd(UnitSpace unitSpace)</td>
                    <td>Gets the class that sets inline-end (right in LTR) margin.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Margin.Block(UnitSpace unitSpace)</td>
                    <td>Gets the class that sets block-direction (top/bottom) margin.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Margin.BlockStart(UnitSpace unitSpace)</td>
                    <td>Gets the class that sets block-start (top) margin.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Margin.BlockEnd(UnitSpace unitSpace)</td>
                    <td>Gets the class that sets block-end (bottom) margin.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
